mk(1, 'nomenclature', 'The correct IUPAC name of [Co(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>6</sub>]Cl<sub>3</sub> is', 'hexaamminecobalt(III) chloride', ['hexaaminecobalt(III) chloride', 'hexaamminecobalt(II) chloride', 'cobalt(III) hexaammine chloride'], '<p>Ligands are named first (NH<sub>3</sub> = ammine, with two m), then the metal with its oxidation state in Roman numerals. Charge: x + 0 = +3 (three Cl<sup>-</sup> outside), so Co(III). The cation is named before the anion.</p>');
